./input/gh-1435/ticket.json:5:    "description": "# Sub-issue 1 — developmentMode config knob: config surface + safe fallback (zero behavior change)\n\n## Goal — one sentence\n**The dev leg reads and validates a new `developmentMode` config field** — and until later issues wire `plan`/`adaptive`, every value executes today's default semantics, so nothing breaks for existing workflows.\n\n## Why this framing\nThe parameter set must be DESCRIBED and ACCEPTED now (config surface frozen early, workflows can adopt the field safely), while the behavior behind `plan`/`adaptive` does not exist yet in the engine — an unknown feature must be inert, not half-wired. Missing field = `default` = exactly today's behavior.\n\n## Config surface (this issue freezes it; later issues wire slices)\n```jsonc\n// params.customParams, per leg workflow config (precedent: customParams.feedbackLoop)\n\"developmentMode\": \"default\" | \"plan\" | \"adaptive\",\n\"developmentModeConfig\": { /* slices: plan / adaptive / spawn — spec'd in the epic, parsed permissive */ }\n```\n\n## Architecture / invariants\n- Resolution order: `params.customParams.developmentMode` → validate ∈ {default, plan, adaptive} → resolved mode.\n- **Invariant I1 (safety): missing, null, empty, or invalid value ⇒ resolved mode = `default`** (+ one warning log line naming the offending value). Nothing throws; the leg never fails because of this field.\n- **Invariant I2 (inertness): in this issue the resolved mode does not reach any behavior path** — appendix injection, thresholds, spawn: none exist yet. The resolved mode is logged (run summary/log line: `developmentMode=<resolved>`) for observability only.\n- `developmentModeConfig` is parsed permissively: unknown keys ignored (forward compatibility), wrong types logged-and-ignored.\n- Resolution lives in the same layer that reads `customParams.feedbackLoop` (single place; no per-workflow-file duplication).\n\n## Acceptance criteria (testable)\n- **AC1** — no `developmentMode` key → resolved `default`, no warning, byte-identical leg behavior vs pre-change engine (golden log diff).\n- **AC2** — `\"developmentMode\": \"plan\"` → resolved `plan`, logged, but executed leg is byte-identical to `default` in this issue (inertness test).\n- **AC3** — invalid values (`\"adaptive?\"`, `123`, `\"\"`, `null`) → resolved `default` + exactly one warning naming the value.\n- **AC4** — `developmentModeConfig` with unknown keys / wrong types → ignored + warning; leg proceeds.\n- **AC5** — case handling: `\"PLAN\"` (documented: case-sensitive, lowercase only) → invalid → `default` + warning (pin the choice; do not silently normalize).\n\n## Test plan\n- `UT-*` resolver unit tests: table of raw configs → resolved mode + warning count (AC1–AC5).\n- `IT-*` leg-config parse integration: fixture workflow configs (with/without the field, junk values) through the real config-reading path.\n- `E2E-*` one live leg on the test repo with the field set to `adaptive` + `shadowMode`-style logging — run completes green, logs show resolved mode, behavior identical to default.\n- `REG-*` regression guard: run the existing 6 test-repo workflow configs through the new resolver — zero behavior drift (golden outputs); **red REG blocks merge even when IT/E2E are green**.\n\n## Non-goals\n- No behavior behind `plan`/`adaptive` (sub-issues 2–3).\n- No spawn config semantics (sub-issue 5) — only the parse-permissively rule applies here.\n- No migration tooling: workflows adopt the field at their own pace; absence is the supported steady state.\n\n## Open questions\n- Resolved (owner, 2026-11-10): invalid-value warning goes to the **run log only** — ticket comments are user-visible noise for a no-op field.\n\n## References\n- Epic: `00-EPIC-configurable-development-modes.md` (config surface, evidence).\n- Engine precedent: `params.customParams.feedbackLoop` handling in `dmtools-agents/js/developTicketAndCreatePR.js`."
